Come out and show yourself, Straw Hat!

263
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:06,272
Stop being such a pansy!

264
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:08,960
Get out here and fight me already!

265
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:11,857
I don't know how that
weirdo figured out my name.

266
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:13,657
I've never seen him before in my life!

267
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:15,177
Didn't you hear what those people said?

268
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:17,260
I think that guy might be Franky!

269
00:16:17,540 --> 00:16:19,080
Then we found him!

270
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:24,100
He's the one who beat up Usopp!

271
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:27,440
This money belongs to us now, understand?

272
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:39,850
No!

273
00:16:39,933 --> 00:16:40,763
Give it back!

274
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:42,880
Give it back!

275
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:46,580
It wasn't for him!

276
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:48,250
Luffy!

277
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:53,250
Hey!

278
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:54,500
Bikini guy!

279
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:55,620
Hold on a sec!

280
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:04,360
That's me!

281
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:05,620
I'm Straw Hat!

282
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:08,400
There's still no information?

283
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,020
What's going on?

284
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:11,630
Everyone?

285
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:16,378
So what's the word?

286
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:25,377
You may enter, but try to keep your
voices down, please. Then he...

287
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:26,500
he's okay?

288
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:29,680
His injuries are still serious, but Mr.

289
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,360
Iceberg has finally
regained consciousness.

290
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,320
That's great news!

291
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:38,080
Come on, let's see how he's doing.

292
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:41,480
You're okay!

293
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:45,180
Well, I've been better, I suppose.

294
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,677
All things considered,
you're pretty lucky.

295
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:49,877
Anyway, you just focus on getting better.

296
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:53,817
In the meantime, you can count on us
to take care of the shipyard, okay?

297
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:54,920
Yes, of course.

298
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:59,517
Now I need to talk to you about the
people who broke into my room last night.

299
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:00,430
Uh, yeah.

300
00:18:00,513 --> 00:18:02,817
Well, that's still under
investigation, I'm afraid.

301
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:05,080
No, I remember them. Huh?

302
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:10,800
There were two.

303
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:15,748
One of them was a large man who was
wearing a mask, and the other was a woman.

304
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:19,000
Tall, with long black hair.

305
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,400
I could never forget those eyes.

306
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:26,920
It has to be her.

307
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:39,160
I can't believe what I just heard. Mr.

308
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:40,757
Iceberg's awake, everyone!

309
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:43,097
It looks like our mayor's gonna be okay!

310
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:44,880
Is that true? All right!

311
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:48,360
I knew he'd make it! Yes!

312
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:53,900
So you're Luffy, huh?

313
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:57,120
Didn't expect you to look so shrimpy.

314
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,157
I got a bone to pick with you, kid.

315
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:04,857
It seems you and your
gang had a little party at

316
00:19:04,940 --> 00:19:07,817
my place while I was gone
when I came home now?

317
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:10,317
What did I see my house
is up to shreds and my

318
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:13,077
gang was on its knees and
it's all thanks to Luffy!

319
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:18,220
I'll make this as plain as can be when you
mess with my voice you mess with Franky!

320
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:21,777
I'd hate to be you right
now cuz I'm on one hell

321
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:24,860
of a roll this week and
ain't nobody gonna stop me!

322
00:19:25,020 --> 00:19:27,577
Now you can cry if you
like but either way!

323
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:32,157
I'm gonna pound you so hard even your own
mother won't recognize you when I'm done.

324
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,880
Shut up! Huh?

325
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:35,180
You jerk!

326
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:39,160
Give us our 200 million berries
back already! You hear me?

327
00:19:39,820 --> 00:19:40,650
Huh?

328
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:43,040
You want your money back, you say?

329
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:47,420
Well, that's a damn shame,
because I'm afraid I spent it all!

330
00:19:48,220 --> 00:19:50,780
You pirates are all a
bunch of sore losers.

331
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:52,917
Don't act all high and mighty when you

332
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,377
probably just stole the
money from someone else.

333
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:56,557
The money doesn't matter.

334
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:58,758
Maybe not to you, but it does to me.

335
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,937
All I care about now is getting revenge,

336
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:04,400
So money or no money,
I'm gonna make you pay!

337
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:08,000
You're stealing my lines, you bastard!

338
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:10,137
Are you trying to make me mad?

339
00:20:10,220 --> 00:20:11,050
Whatever!

340
00:20:11,133 --> 00:20:12,745
Just come down here and fight!

341
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:14,110
Uh-oh!

342
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,906
Everybody get out of the way!

343
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:19,260
Frankie's going on a rampage! Come away!

344
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,657
Is he holding his breath or something?

345
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:28,570
Weird.

346
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:57,600
He just spit fire!

347
00:20:57,740 --> 00:20:59,799
Yeah, I can see that much, but how?

348
00:21:01,540 --> 00:21:02,940
Oh? You scared?

349
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:04,513
Having second thoughts?

350
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:05,470
Careful!

351
00:21:05,553 --> 00:21:07,817
If he can do that, he might
have Devil Fruit powers!

352
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:09,959
Okay, but that doesn't really help!

353
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:24,597
If that guy did eat a Devil Fruit, he
wouldn't just jump in the water for no reason.

354
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,510
Would he?

355
00:21:25,593 --> 00:21:28,377
Maybe nobody told him that if
you tried to swim, you'd die.

356
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:29,877
That'd be pretty pathetic,

357
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:33,842
but at least it would save us the
trouble of fighting that weirdo.

358
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:49,140
I guess he can't swim!

359
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:50,920
Lucky didn't drown, huh?

360
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:54,380
I didn't eat no Devil Fruit.

361
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:55,716
You think I'm crazy?

362
00:21:58,460 --> 00:21:59,290
Huh?

363
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:02,660
Doesn't matter to me!

364
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:04,760
Can't surprise me.

365
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:07,352
I heard about that little power of yours.

366
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:12,410
Stronger!

367
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,270
What?

368
00:22:28,460 --> 00:22:29,600
Oh, man.

369
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:45,350
Lupi!

370
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:48,530
Hey!

371
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:49,720
Are you okay?

372
00:22:57,560 --> 00:23:00,854
If you don't have Devil Fruit
powers, then what are you?

373
00:23:01,060 --> 00:23:01,890
Huh?

374
00:23:01,973 --> 00:23:04,900
You poor saps don't know
anything now, do you?

375
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:06,640
All right, then.

376
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:07,980
I'll humor you.

377
00:23:09,340 --> 00:23:12,120
I'm just a normal guy
with some extra parts.

378
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,540
A cyborg, you might say.

379
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:25,997
One of the Straw Hats did this?

380
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:28,577
Sure about that?

381
00:23:28,660 --> 00:23:30,057
Of all people? Yes.

382
00:23:30,140 --> 00:23:33,097
And my personal investigation
led to the same result.

383
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:37,657
To make sure I had Lucy, contact the
government to confirm her identity and bounty.

384
00:23:37,740 --> 00:23:39,177
Yes.

385
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:43,297
They said she's a notorious criminal, so
it's no surprise that she'd do something.

386
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:45,480
Catastrophe to our boss! Cuckoo!

387
00:23:52,660 --> 00:23:55,337
And our next course of
action is crystal clear.

388
00:23:55,420 --> 00:23:58,677
We gotta find those rapscallions
and show them what's what.

389
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:00,577
What in the hell were they thinking?

390
00:24:00,660 --> 00:24:03,317
Don't tell me they're pissed off
because we wouldn't fix their ship.

391
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:04,635
I wonder that myself.

392
00:24:04,820 --> 00:24:07,057
But regardless of what
their motivations might be,

393
00:24:07,140 --> 00:24:10,357
the bottom line is that they're the
culprits and they need to be dealt with.

394
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,270
In other words,

395
00:24:11,353 --> 00:24:13,417
we should just capture the
Straw Hats and interrogate them

396
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:16,657
ourselves instead of wasting time
trying to figure this crap out.

397
00:24:16,740 --> 00:24:18,357
None of this makes sense to me,

398
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:22,146
but anyone who messes with
Galley-La is gonna have hell to pay.

399
00:24:31,820 --> 00:24:33,080
Hey! There's trouble!

400
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:35,160
Shut up, Tile Stone!

401
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:36,777
You're way the hell too loud!

402
00:24:36,860 --> 00:24:37,690
You fools!

403
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,800
You're just as loud as he is!

404
00:24:40,380 --> 00:24:41,210
Oh!

405
00:24:41,293 --> 00:24:42,937
I didn't know you were up already, Mr.

406
00:24:43,020 --> 00:24:44,340
Iceberg! That's great!

407
00:24:47,100 --> 00:24:50,557
He may be awake, but that doesn't
mean you should scream his ears off.

408
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:52,640
Take it down a notch or two, okay?

409
00:24:53,140 --> 00:24:53,970
I'm sorry!

410
00:24:54,053 --> 00:24:55,740
I can't help it! I swear!

411
00:24:57,500 --> 00:24:58,676
Oh, I almost forgot!

412
00:24:58,760 --> 00:25:00,057
I had a turn or something!

413
00:25:00,140 --> 00:25:01,493
Fine, but stay outside.

414
00:25:01,780 --> 00:25:02,997
You can tell me from over there.

415
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:04,977
We got trouble with that Straw Hat guy!

416
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:06,077
I don't know what happened,

417
00:25:06,160 --> 00:25:10,017
but he got in a big fight with Franky and
they're both wrecking up the shipyard.

418
00:25:10,100 --> 00:25:12,982
If we don't stop them,
who knows what they'll do?

419
00:25:16,340 --> 00:25:17,500
Straw Hat again?

420
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:20,254
But at least we know where to find him.

421
00:25:23,100 --> 00:25:24,360
He's got some nerve.

422
00:25:24,880 --> 00:25:27,821
I'll teach that punk to
show his face on our turf.

423
00:25:30,860 --> 00:25:33,437
Now you can finally have
a bit of peace and quiet.

424
00:25:33,520 --> 00:25:35,402
Let them take care of Straw Hat.

425
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:38,437
I'll be watching over you in the meantime.

426
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:40,167
So there's no need to worry.

427
00:25:47,160 --> 00:25:48,400
Come, come.

428
00:25:56,920 --> 00:25:59,037
Watch out, it's coming down!

429
00:25:59,120 --> 00:26:00,777
It turns to the ship.

430
00:26:00,860 --> 00:26:03,980
Stop it, go fight somewhere else.

431
00:26:05,160 --> 00:26:05,990
Ah!

432
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:11,190
Luffy!

433
00:26:11,380 --> 00:26:14,217
Tear him to pieces and then
they can put some pants on!

434
00:26:14,300 --> 00:26:15,200
Hey, bro.

435
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:17,560
You gotta put on a good show.

436
00:26:25,420 --> 00:26:27,797
You're a lot tougher
than I thought you'd be.

437
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:30,320
But I'm still gonna beat you, bikini guy!

438
00:26:31,880 --> 00:26:33,077
If you say so,

439
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:37,336
Now it's gonna take a long-ass time
with those weenie attacks of yours.

440
00:26:48,420 --> 00:26:49,580
Weapons left!

441
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:55,540
Go, go!

442
00:27:06,300 --> 00:27:07,420
I can't see.

443
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:09,442
It seems like they both got hit.

444
00:27:09,840 --> 00:27:11,480
No, look who it is.

445
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,420
Who just punched me?

446
00:27:19,760 --> 00:27:21,000
This is too easy.

447
00:27:21,240 --> 00:27:25,337
If you knew what was good for you, you
would have skipped town a long time ago.

448
00:27:25,420 --> 00:27:26,655
You're in for it now.

449
00:27:33,460 --> 00:27:34,340
Gally-la.

450
00:27:34,740 --> 00:27:36,564
Great, that's just what I need.

451
00:27:36,700 --> 00:27:39,477
All right, the guys from
Doc Ward finally made it.

452
00:27:39,560 --> 00:27:41,957
Lock those loosers up
and throw away the key.

453
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:42,870
Whoo!

454
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:56,318
All right, the four men will
take care of these guys.

455
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:57,840
That was close.

456
00:27:58,080 --> 00:28:01,357
If they didn't show up, the whole
shipyard was gonna get totaled.

457
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:02,720
Wow, lucky break.

458
00:28:02,940 --> 00:28:05,477
Finally, someone can put
a stop to this nonsense.

459
00:28:05,560 --> 00:28:07,266
I bet they hate Franky, too.

460
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:09,739
I'd butt out of this if I were you.

461
00:28:09,920 --> 00:28:12,317
Once these fists start
rocking and rolling,

462
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:15,337
they don't discriminate between
pirates and shipwrights.

463
00:28:15,420 --> 00:28:17,977
And that goes for other
people's property, too.

464
00:28:18,060 --> 00:28:20,697
Surely you don't expect us
to stand here gobsmacked

465
00:28:20,780 --> 00:28:22,898
while you wreck our entire shipyard.

466
00:28:23,380 --> 00:28:24,817
I'm warning you, Franky!

467
00:28:24,900 --> 00:28:28,057
If you don't pay for these repairs
and berries, you'll pay in blood!

468
00:28:28,140 --> 00:28:29,877
All right, Tile Stone, calm down.

469
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:32,548
We can take care of
Franky some other time.

470
00:28:32,880 --> 00:28:36,233
We've got more important
business to deal with right now.

471
00:28:37,700 --> 00:28:39,880
Yeah, I'm looking at you, Straw Hat.

472
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:42,237
You know exactly what I'm talking about.

473
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:45,617
I don't know if you're brave or
stupid, but either way, you're dead.

474
00:28:45,700 --> 00:28:46,530
Wait, what?

475
00:28:46,613 --> 00:28:50,071
We just came here because we
heard the news about Ice Pops.

476
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:53,937
Wasn't enough to wreck my
house and beat up my boys, huh?

477
00:28:54,020 --> 00:28:54,850
What's wrong?

478
00:28:54,933 --> 00:28:57,677
Don't feel like a man unless you're
pounding the crap out of ship rights, too?

479
00:28:57,760 --> 00:29:00,457
I know the puberty can make
you do some really crazy stuff,

480
00:29:00,540 --> 00:29:02,917
but wow I don't even know what's going on?

481
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:08,560
So stop making fun of me play innocent
all you like I won't go easy on you!

482
00:29:09,520 --> 00:29:11,140
Romance and Half-Nob!

483
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:15,070
Don't breathe.

484
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:16,830
Don't breathe.

485
00:29:19,720 --> 00:29:20,550
Air drive!

486
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:25,000
Dammit, just go away!

487
00:29:25,380 --> 00:29:27,837
I told you shipwrights to
stay out of this, didn't I?

488
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:30,802
I'm the one who owes this
guy a beating, not you!

489
00:29:36,620 --> 00:29:37,620
Go Galilass!

490
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:39,177
Show them what you're made of!

491
00:29:39,260 --> 00:29:42,757
There's no way they can beat the
top five shipwrights in the city!

492
00:29:42,840 --> 00:29:43,670
What?

493
00:29:43,753 --> 00:29:45,757
Why are the shipwrights
fighting against us, too?

494
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:47,040
Makes me itchy.

495
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:51,520
What are you doing?

496
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:54,197
I don't have any reason to fight you guys!

497
00:29:54,280 --> 00:29:55,300
Just hold on!

498
00:30:01,180 --> 00:30:02,010
Look at that.

499
00:30:02,093 --> 00:30:03,400
He's got Devil Fruit power.

500
00:30:14,340 --> 00:30:16,520
Hey, stupid, are you even listening?

501
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:19,329
How many times do I
have to tell you bozos?

502
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:21,960
For the last time.

503
00:30:24,620 --> 00:30:26,820
Straw Hat is mine, dammit!

504
00:30:35,140 --> 00:30:39,017
Sorry, Franky, but we don't have
time for your shenanigans today.

505
00:30:39,100 --> 00:30:41,806
Get the hell out of my
way, you flying monkey!

506
00:30:42,640 --> 00:30:44,522
You're the one who's in the way!

507
00:30:47,980 --> 00:30:49,260
Oh, yeah!

508
00:30:49,980 --> 00:30:51,274
That's our tile stone!

509
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:53,518
He's even stronger than usual today!

510
00:31:04,840 --> 00:31:07,320
Cuckoo! Cuckoo! Cuckoo! Cuckoo!

511
00:31:09,820 --> 00:31:11,980
Hey, stop it!

512
00:31:30,040 --> 00:31:31,980
Damn, you guys are strong!

513
00:31:32,360 --> 00:31:34,831
But I still don't know why we're fighting!

514
00:31:40,360 --> 00:31:44,772
Straw Hat, I think we're the ones who
deserve an explanation here, not you.

515
00:31:46,760 --> 00:31:49,217
Someone broke into
Iceberg's house last night.

516
00:31:49,300 --> 00:31:53,057
Shot him twice in the front and three
times in the back before they left.

517
00:31:53,140 --> 00:31:54,697
They were from your crew.

518
00:31:54,780 --> 00:31:56,100
That can't be!

519
00:31:56,460 --> 00:31:58,160
None of us would do that!

520
00:31:58,340 --> 00:32:00,420
I'm never gonna settle this, am I?

521
00:32:23,140 --> 00:32:24,920
That was Nico Robin.

522
00:32:25,340 --> 00:32:27,660
There's not a single doubt in my mind.

523
00:32:28,200 --> 00:32:31,480
But was that masked man one
of the Straw Hats as well?

524
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,906
And why did they attack
me in the first place?

525
00:32:35,560 --> 00:32:37,560
Surely it wasn't about their ship.

526
00:32:37,820 --> 00:32:41,020
No, they must have been
aiming to steal something.

527
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:46,701
But seeing as they left empty-handed, I
have a good idea what they were looking for.

528
00:32:46,920 --> 00:32:49,817
The question is, if they were
working with the government,

529
00:32:49,900 --> 00:32:52,140
or if they want it for themselves.

530
00:32:52,740 --> 00:32:54,040
Straw Hat Luffy.

531
00:32:55,420 --> 00:32:56,640
This just in!

532
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:57,700
Breaking news!

533
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:02,477
Iceberg has already identified the
culprits from the break-in last night!

534
00:33:02,560 --> 00:33:03,390
What?

535
00:33:03,473 --> 00:33:04,303
Is that true?

536
00:33:04,386 --> 00:33:07,457
Spread the word through the city
and we'll capture them ourselves!

537
00:33:07,540 --> 00:33:11,280
We can't let those criminals
leave Water 7! Who did it?

538
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:17,060
Show no mercy to the monsters
who attacked our mayor!

539
00:33:20,260 --> 00:33:23,680
Capture the Straw Hat Pirates
no matter what it takes!

540
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:28,080
Iceberg was shot?

541
00:33:28,740 --> 00:33:30,020
That's news to me.

542
00:33:34,640 --> 00:33:36,600
Dad, can't be! We.

543
00:33:39,220 --> 00:33:40,050
No way!

544
00:33:40,133 --> 00:33:41,797
We didn't shoot Ice Pops.

545
00:33:41,880 --> 00:33:42,777
That's just crazy!

546
00:33:42,860 --> 00:33:45,897
There were two people who broke
into his room and attacked him.

547
00:33:45,980 --> 00:33:47,457
He may have been hurt.

548
00:33:47,540 --> 00:33:50,037
But that doesn't mean he didn't
get a good look at him first.

549
00:33:50,120 --> 00:33:52,860
One of them was a big guy with a mask on.

550
00:33:53,440 --> 00:33:56,400
The other was a tall
woman with black hair.

551
00:33:57,560 --> 00:33:59,837
Iceberg told us he recognized her and the

552
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:02,802
government confirmed she's
a member of your crew.

553
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:06,600
The archaeologist, Nico Robin.

554
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:09,180
You're lying!

555
00:34:13,900 --> 00:34:15,600
I won't ask you why.

556
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:19,388
Maybe your crew came to Water
7 on a mission to kill Iceberg.

557
00:34:19,540 --> 00:34:22,017
Or maybe you really did
want your ship repaired

558
00:34:22,100 --> 00:34:25,037
and attacked him on a whim
after we turned you down.

559
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:28,238
I don't know how you pirates
think, and I don't care.

560
00:34:29,140 --> 00:34:33,669
Point is, you tried to kill my boss,
and now I'm gonna have to take you down.

561
00:34:33,900 --> 00:34:35,547
So he's one of the culprits?

562
00:34:35,800 --> 00:34:36,900
Tie him up, Polly!

563
00:34:37,060 --> 00:34:38,377
Don't let that pirate go!

564
00:34:38,460 --> 00:34:39,460
This is bad.

565
00:34:40,040 --> 00:34:43,700
So he got shot five times,
but Iceberg's still alive?

566
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:45,257
Don't look so surprised.

567
00:34:45,340 --> 00:34:46,977
That guy's as tough as nails.

568
00:34:47,060 --> 00:34:49,260
But if they tried it once,

569
00:34:49,500 --> 00:34:53,559
then these scumbags might try to go
after Iceberg a second time, too.

570
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:56,080
So we're gonna settle this now.

571
00:34:59,820 --> 00:35:04,440
Dead or alive, the world
government doesn't care either way.

572
00:35:04,700 --> 00:35:07,497
This is what it means to
have a bounty on your head.

573
00:35:07,580 --> 00:35:11,756
Therefore, you can't complain, no
matter how terrible your fate may be.

574
00:35:12,420 --> 00:35:16,420
You've broken the law, and now the
law has turned its back on you.

575
00:35:17,300 --> 00:35:18,200
That's right.

576
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:21,780
We chose to live this way.

577
00:35:22,660 --> 00:35:25,260
We're all outlaws, but I don't care.

578
00:35:26,220 --> 00:35:27,050
You're wrong!

579
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:29,517
If you knew Robin, you wouldn't say that!

580
00:35:29,600 --> 00:35:30,600
Take that back!

581
00:35:32,360 --> 00:35:34,500
Luffy, let me talk to Ice Pops.

582
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:36,171
This has to be a mistake.

583
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:37,977
There's no way it was Robin.

584
00:35:38,060 --> 00:35:40,397
We'd be fools to let
you anywhere near him.

585
00:35:40,480 --> 00:35:42,833
Criminals have no right to make demands.

586
00:35:43,380 --> 00:35:44,240
He's right!

587
00:35:44,520 --> 00:35:45,873
Shut up the conference!

588
00:35:46,440 --> 00:35:49,558
Those bastards can't get
away with shooting our hero!

589
00:35:49,700 --> 00:35:51,520
Send him to the gallows!

590
00:35:52,300 --> 00:35:53,240
Hey, wait!

591
00:35:53,580 --> 00:35:55,820
Just calm down! Hold on!

592
00:35:56,440 --> 00:35:57,270
What?

593
00:35:57,360 --> 00:35:59,080
You can't fool me, Missy!

594
00:35:59,220 --> 00:36:01,117
I saw you with that Straw Hat guy!

595
00:36:01,200 --> 00:36:03,717
I bet you're one of the
criminals, aren't ya?

596
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:05,200
Really? Yeah!

597
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:08,357
She was riding along with him
on a yagra when he got here!

598
00:36:08,440 --> 00:36:09,840
We've got you now!

599
00:36:10,120 --> 00:36:12,120
You're gonna get what you deserve!

600
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:14,640
Stop it! Let me go!

601
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:16,390
Nami!

602
00:36:16,540 --> 00:36:19,137
Word of this is going
to spread like wildfire.

603
00:36:19,220 --> 00:36:22,080
There's no place to run
and no place to hide.

604
00:36:22,520 --> 00:36:24,040
It's the end of the road.

605
00:36:24,280 --> 00:36:26,220
You pirates are going down.

606
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:29,280
Extra, extra, read all about it.

607
00:36:29,400 --> 00:36:32,517
The Straw Hat Pirates were the
culprits in the attack against Mr.

608
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:33,430
Iceberg.

609
00:36:34,320 --> 00:36:37,697
The Water Water newspaper
will purchase any information

610
00:36:37,780 --> 00:36:40,427
related to their current
location or actions.

611
00:36:41,900 --> 00:36:44,757
We know that the culprits
are still here on the island,

612
00:36:44,840 --> 00:36:46,840
so be sure to stay on the lookout!

613
00:36:47,440 --> 00:36:52,160
We must band together to hunt down the
Straw Hats and send them to the gallows!

614
00:36:52,280 --> 00:36:53,110
Yeah!
